        "summary":  "The article lays out an eight-step security framework for enterprises deploying AI agents, organized around three pillars: constraining agent capabilities, controlling data and behavior, and proving governance. It warns that relying on prompt-level safeguards alone is insufficient and that each agent should run with the narrowest possible permissions scoped to a specific user role. The framework aligns with NIST, OWASP, Google SAIF, and EU AI Act guidance.",
